message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "collect-settings: build, encode and decode ODK Collect / KoboCollect configuration QR codes"
version: "0.1.3"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23579946
repository-code: "https://github.com/milkway/collect-settings"
url: "https://crates.io/crates/collect-settings"
keywords:
  - ODK Collect
  - KoboCollect
  - QR code
  - survey
  - data collection
  - Rust
authors:
  - family-names: Leite
    given-names: "André"
    email: leite@castlab.org
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4718-9766"
abstract: >-
  collect-settings builds, encodes and decodes the configuration QR codes of
  ODK Collect and KoboCollect (settings JSON, zlib-compressed and
  base64-encoded, rendered as a QR code), as a Rust library with JavaScript
  bindings published to npm.
